  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Chapter nine, lesson one."
   ],
   [
    2.135,
    "Energy flow, catabolism and redox."
   ],
   [
    5.273,
    "Sunlight pours down onto a leaf."
   ],
   [
    7.669,
    "The leaf captures some of that light and stores it as the chemical energy of sugar."
   ],
   [
    12.852,
    "And sooner or later, every living thing lets that energy go as heat, which never comes back."
   ],
   [
    18.971,
    "Energy flows through an ecosystem: in as light, out as heat."
   ],
   [
    23.607,
    "Now follow an animal that eats the leaf."
   ],
   [
    26.185,
    "Its cells must turn the energy in food into something they can spend."
   ],
   [
    30.547,
    "Zoom in further, and inside the cell we find the mitochondrion, where most of that work happens."
   ],
   [
    36.576,
    "This chapter follows that process, one step at a time."
   ]
  ]
 },
