  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "Plants and other producers use light energy to build organic molecules and oxygen out of carbon dioxide and water."
   ],
   [
    7.708,
    "Cellular respiration, in the mitochondria, takes those organic molecules and oxygen, and breaks the molecules down."
   ],
   [
    15.547,
    "What is left over is carbon dioxide and water, and these go straight back to photosynthesis."
   ],
   [
    21.354,
    "So matter goes round in a circle."
   ],
   [
    23.594,
    "The breakdown generates A T P, the molecule that powers most cellular work."
   ],
   [
    29.219,
    "And part of the energy escapes as heat."
   ],
   [
    31.732,
    "Matter cycles, but energy only flows through, one way."
   ]
  ]
 },
