  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "Breaking organic molecules down is a catabolic pathway, and it is exergonic: it releases free energy."
   ],
   [
    7.591,
    "It yields that energy by oxidizing the fuel."
   ],
   [
    10.703,
    "In a moment we will see exactly what that word means."
   ],
   [
    13.893,
    "There are three ways to do it."
   ],
   [
    15.599,
    "Fermentation is a partial breakdown of sugar, and it happens without oxygen."
   ],
   [
    20.612,
    "Aerobic respiration consumes organic molecules and oxygen, and yields A T P."
   ],
   [
    26.914,
    "Anaerobic respiration is similar, but it consumes some compound other than oxygen."
   ],
   [
    32.175,
    "The words cellular respiration cover both kinds of respiration, but they are often used to mean the aerobic one."
   ],
   [
    39.128,
    "That is the one we will follow."
   ]
  ]
 },
